Retry WebGPU adapter/device requests so AMD and Intel GPUs can load.

Keep Subgroups on every limit retry and re-derive shader capabilities from
the granted device. Dropping Subgroups while the adapter still reported the
feature compiled WGSL with `enable subgroups` and Chrome rejected it
(`extension 'subgroups' is not allowed`), which aborted WASM onto CPU.

Never guess a subgroup size: unknown/zero disables subgroups (workgroup
reduction shaders) instead of assuming 32/64. A wrong MAX_SUBGROUP_SIZE
silently mistranslates. There is no debug override that can force 64 on
32-wide hardware.

After the device is granted, run a cheap known-answer probe (workgroup add
plus a subgroup_size readback). A size mismatch drops subgroups in-process;
an add mismatch disables WebGPU.

Also: no GGML_ASSERT on a failed requestDevice; parseable device-ready /
device-features / device-limits / correctness-probe log lines; debug
profiles that actually constrain the wasm request (no-f16, reject-max-limits).

See ggml-org/llama.cpp#21744, #23844 and Chromium crbug 369219127.

